{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Abhaya","html":"<article id='thag1.26'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.26 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.26 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Tatiyavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Three </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Abhayattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Abhaya </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Sutvā subhāsitaṁ vācaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Having heard the fine words </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>buddhassādiccabandhuno; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>of the Buddha, Kinsman of the Sun, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Paccabyadhiṁ hi nipuṇaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I penetrated the subtle truth, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>vālaggaṁ usunā yathā”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>like a hair-tip with an arrow. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Abhayo thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
